ted = [\"LLR-207\", \"SR-156\"]","+copied = [\"docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml\", \"docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml\"]"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-996\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":2222,"oldLines":8,"newStart":2222,"newLines":8,"lines":[" sr_refs = [\"SR-156\"]"," title = \"The verdict record: what carries a governing verdict, and what binds it to the tree it judged\""," module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/verdict.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/station.py;project-trajectory/scripts/integrate.py\"","-code_symbol = \"RECORD_PREFIXES/fold_listing/tree_identity/refresh_subject/refresh_attestation/format_bar_green/bar_attestation/tests_digest/mechanical_close_attestation/work_tip/governing_rev/governing_identity/format_trailer/parse_trailer/round_file/session_log/format_scope/gating_span/filing_refusal/branch_paths/logged_rounds/round_entries/branch_entries/tree_already_judged/declared_phases/phases_owed/round_count/_closed_wi_ids/mechanical_close_subject/format_branch_trailer/branch_trailers;attest/_attest_preflight/_attest_message/_lane_off_trunk/_harness_floor_refusal/_attest_commit/_bar_refusal/_review_bar_command/_run_review_bar/_unstaged_dirt/_AttestPlan\"","-detail = \"\"\"tree_identity folds raw NUL-delimited `git ls-tree -r -z` entries after dropping docs/reviews/, docs/log.d/ and docs/iteration/, and returns a 64-hex SHA-256 identity. fold_listing accepts bytes and preserves every path byte so display quoting or decoding cannot merge distinct work trees. A Bar-Green attestation is exactly one column-0 label line, `Bar-Green: tree=<40 hex> work=<40 hex> bar=<review|landing|no-bar> tests=<64 hex|none> <summary>`; its verifier returns fields only when tree and work equal the commit's own tree and first parent and bar is in that set. tests carries none for an empty named test-path set; otherwise it carries the SHA-256 of that set after path separators and leading ./ are normalized, duplicates are removed, and the paths are joined in sorted order. Thus one set in any order or spelling has one value, and a different set has a different value. refresh_attestation admits a refresh subject only with that verified attestation and bar landing or no-bar, so work_tip never peels a review attestation as a refresh; the read-only identity walk still steps through any commit whose non-record identity equals its parent, including an empty review attestation. One producer writes every attestation: it fixes the staged tree before the bar, refuses a red bar or one that leaves the index or worktree off that tree, and restores the index on every failed write; its line joins the message's final trailer block. The attest route refuses before the bar when commit hooks are off, the primary checkout holds the branch, the worktree is dirty (including untracked files), the review-bar declaration is absent or empty, the message carries the label, or the harness floor refuses; it reads the review bar and derived test set from the attested lane's own declarations, with no default, and refuses before the bar when derivation refuses; a refusal leaves the branch and index unchanged. On the attest route the producer runs the review bar then the derived files, records their digest in the unchanged grammar, and prints the set, listed evidence and reported gaps. A trailer without bar is not read. work_tip peels only a verified refresh at the tip for the reset path; governing_rev is read-only and walks across commits whose non-record identity equals their first parent's, peeling any DISPOSABLE commit it meets to reach one those commits would otherwise hide, and ending at the first commit whose identity differs from its parent's or at its absent-parent and depth bounds - so a branch with no disposable commit under it still walks. TWO commit classes are disposable and the read-only walk peels BOTH: the station's REFRESH, admitted by refresh_attestation, and the machinery's OWN adjudication close, admitted by mechanical_close_attestation against exactly one parent and a no-renames changed-path stream lying wholly under docs/work/. That stream must pair deleted specs from exactly ONE docs/work/active/<branch>/ with additions of the same filenames under docs/work/complete/, and ONLY the move itself may create or destroy: an addition or deletion under docs/work/ that is not one half of a recognised move refuses the whole commit, since peeling it would measure a spec's injection or an archived row's destruction at the parent, where no reviewer saw it. Modifications ride along unrestricted, because a close's inbound relink rewrites other rows in place and only ever modifies. A mechanical close admits exactly one moved row; any other shape declines to peel toward more review. Its subject must equal the writer's composed subject exactly, so a public prefix/suffix with a forged middle is not an attestation. The one-row clause refuses an empty close, which has no deletion, and every multi-row close; one deletion implies one source branch; and the subject composer takes a single id and refuses anything else, so no empty-id subject is ever composed. One property admits the two classes and it is not two rules: both are machine-authored end to end, and both move the tree without the lane having changed what it CLAIMS - docs/work/ is deliberately inside the identity because a spec's own claims are what a verdict is about, and the close carries those claims through unchanged. Every arm of both verifications fails toward REVIEW, since declining to peel measures at a later rev and can never ask for LESS - though not always for more: on the empty close the refused commit is identity-preserving, so the walk-through step reaches the same rev the peel would have, and the refusal guards this function's contract rather than any answer the gate gives. The two peels are NOT the same peel: work_tip calls refresh_attestation directly rather than through the shared disposable test, so a mechanical close is never removed by the destructive reset path, which may only ever drop a refresh sitting literally on the tip. governing_identity composes governing_rev and tree_identity for the branch tip or an explicit revision, including a round's reviewed commit and a trailer's carrier; the branch argument is a branch NAME, because the peel verifies a refresh commit against the branch it names and no refresh subject names HEAD. format_scope records a REVIEW session scope as full, narrow or final base..sha; gating_span admits a fresh full scope in either mode, or a final scope only where reviewer retention is on and final_reviewer is persisted; a narrow scope and a retained full scope never admit. logged_rounds joins branch-scoped round files to coordinator session logs by train and ordinal, and each round's review phase is the JOINED LOG's declared phase rather than the one its own filename carries, so a file cannot claim a phase its session did not serve; a joined key whose logs declare more than one review phase yields no round. It retains only a gating span whose base equals the caller's claim base and whose reviewed sha the round file names. round_entries retains only rounds whose reviewed revision governs the identity under judgement and emits phase, ordinal and verdict entries through an injected parser. filing_refusal applies one filing check: the first physical line is exactly the Reviewed full-sha opener (a CR ending is allowed; no leading blank or whitespace is), exactly one canonical VERDICT line, a finding count matching the file, and a change request naming a finding. An unreadable or refused round is an entry with no verdict, so it is the phase's latest word rather than an older verdict being used. tree_already_judged is true only for an entry carrying a verdict and false with no base. declared_phases clamps the configured independent-review count to the available review phases. phases_owed returns declared phases whose latest entry is missing or invalid evidence; a dissent is served. round_count returns the largest per-phase entry count at one governing identity, so a multi-phase review cycle counts once and changed work starts a new count. format_trailer and parse_trailer carry `Review-Verdict: APPROVE|CHANGES-REQUESTED rounds=<N> tree=<64 hex>`. branch_trailers verifies each carrier against its governing identity and returns the ordered attestation sequence per tree. Readers treat unavailable repository answers according to their own fail-closed contract.\"\"\"","+code_symbol = \"RECORD_PREFIXES/fold_listing/tree_identity/refresh_subject/refresh_attestation/format_bar_green/bar_attestation/tests_digest/normal_test_paths/last_review_record/mechanical_close_attestation/work_tip/governing_rev/governing_identity/format_trailer/parse_trailer/round_file/session_log/format_scope/gating_span/filing_refusal/branch_paths/logged_rounds/round_entries/branch_entries/tree_already_judged/declared_phases/phases_owed/round_count/_closed_wi_ids/mechanical_close_subject/format_branch_trailer/branch_trailers;attest/_attest_preflight/_attest_message/_lane_off_trunk/_harness_floor_refusal/_attest_commit/_bar_refusal/_lane_mark_refusal/_run_review_bar/_unstaged_dirt/_AttestPlan\"","+detail = \"\"\"tree_identity folds raw NUL-delimited `git ls-tree -r -z` entries after dropping docs/reviews/, docs/log.d/ and docs/iteration/, and returns a 64-hex SHA-256 identity. fold_listing accepts bytes and preserves every path byte so display quoting or decoding cannot merge distinct work trees. A Bar-Green attestation is exactly one column-0 label line, `Bar-Green: tree=<40 hex> work=<40 hex> bar=<review|landing|no-bar> tests=<64 hex|none> <summary>`; its verifier returns fields only when tree and work equal the commit's own tree and first parent and bar is in that set. tests carries none for an empty named test-path set; otherwise it carries the SHA-256 of that set after path separators and leading ./ are normalized, duplicates are removed, and the paths are joined in sorted order. Thus one set in any order or spelling has one value, and a different set has a different value. refresh_attestation admits a refresh subject only with that verified attestation and bar landing or no-bar, so work_tip never peels a review attestation as a refresh; the read-only identity walk still steps through any commit whose non-record identity equals its parent, including an empty review attestation. One producer writes every attestation: it fixes the staged tree before the bar, refuses a red bar or one that leaves the index or worktree off that tree, and restores the index on every failed write; its line joins the message's final trailer block. The attest route refuses before the bar when commit hooks are off, the primary checkout holds the branch, the worktree is dirty (including untracked files), the review-bar declaration is absent or empty, the message carries the label, or the harness floor refuses; it reads the review bar and derived test set from the attested lane's own declarations, with no default, and refuses before the bar when derivation refuses; a refusal leaves the branch and index unchanged. On the attest route the producer runs the review bar then the derived files, records their digest in the unchanged grammar, and prints the set, listed evidence and reported gaps. A trailer without bar is not read. work_tip peels only a verified refresh at the tip for the reset path; governing_rev is read-only and walks across commits whose non-record identity equals their first parent's, peeling any DISPOSABLE commit it meets to reach one those commits would otherwise hide, and ending at the first commit whose identity differs from its parent's or at its absent-parent and depth bounds - so a branch with no disposable commit under it still walks. TWO commit classes are disposable and the read-only walk peels BOTH: the station's REFRESH, admitted by refresh_attestation, and the machinery's OWN adjudication close, admitted by mechanical_close_attestation against exactly one parent and a no-renames changed-path stream lying wholly under docs/work/. That stream must pair deleted specs from exactly ONE docs/work/active/<branch>/ with additions of the same filenames under docs/work/complete/, and ONLY the move itself may create or destroy: an addition or deletion under docs/work/ that is not one half of a recognised move refuses the whole commit, since peeling it would measure a spec's injection or an archived row's destruction at the parent, where no reviewer saw it. Modifications ride along unrestricted, because a close's inbound relink rewrites other rows in place and only ever modifies. A mechanical close admits exactly one moved row; any other shape declines to peel toward more review. Its subject must equal the writer's composed subject exactly, so a public prefix/suffix with a forged middle is not an attestation. The one-row clause refuses an empty close, which has no deletion, and every multi-row close; one deletion implies one source branch; and the subject composer takes a single id and refuses anything else, so no empty-id subject is ever composed. One property admits the two classes and it is not two rules: both are machine-authored end to end, and both move the tree without the lane having changed what it CLAIMS - docs/work/ is deliberately inside the identity because a spec's own claims are what a verdict is about, and the close carries those claims through unchanged. Every arm of both verifications fails toward REVIEW, since declining to peel measures at a later rev and can never ask for LESS - though not always for more: on the empty close the refused commit is identity-preserving, so the walk-through step reaches the same rev the peel would have, and the refusal guards this function's contract rather than any answer the gate gives. The two peels are NOT the same peel: work_tip calls refresh_attestation directly rather than through the shared disposable test, so a mechanical close is never removed by the destructive reset path, which may only ever drop a refresh sitting literally on the tip. governing_identity composes governing_rev and tree_identity for the branch tip or an explicit revision, including a round's reviewed commit and a trailer's carrier; the branch argument is a branch NAME, because the peel verifies a refresh commit against the branch it names and no refresh subject names HEAD. format_scope records a REVIEW session scope as full, narrow or final base..sha; gating_span admits a fresh full scope in either mode, or a final scope only where reviewer retention is on and final_reviewer is persisted; a narrow scope and a retained full scope never admit. logged_rounds joins branch-scoped round files to coordinator session logs by train and ordinal, and each round's review phase is the JOINED LOG's declared phase rather than the one its own filename carries, so a file cannot claim a phase its session did not serve; a joined key whose logs declare more than one review phase yields no round. It retains only a gating span whose base equals the caller's claim base and whose reviewed sha the round file names. round_entries retains only rounds whose reviewed revision governs the identity under judgement and emits phase, ordinal and verdict entries through an injected parser. filing_refusal applies one filing check: the first physical line is exactly the Reviewed full-sha opener (a CR ending is allowed; no leading blank or whitespace is), exactly one canonical VERDICT line, a finding count matching the file, and a change request naming a finding. An unreadable or refused round is an entry with no verdict, so it is the phase's latest word rather than an older verdict being used. tree_already_judged is true only for an entry carrying a verdict and false with no base. declared_phases clamps the configured independent-review count to the available review phases. phases_owed returns declared phases whose latest entry is missing or invalid evidence; a dissent is served. round_count returns the largest per-phase entry count at one governing identity, so a multi-phase review cycle counts once and changed work starts a new count. format_trailer and parse_trailer carry `Review-Verdict: APPROVE|CHANGES-REQUESTED rounds=<N> tree=<64 hex>`. branch_trailers verifies each carrier against its governing identity and returns the ordered attestation sequence per tree. Readers treat unavailable repository answers according to their own fail-closed contract. The attest route reads the declared expected-failure mark with the review bar from one parse of the attested lane's declarations, with no default, and refuses before either bar when either required declaration is unavailable or its mark transition is refused under LLR-368.\"\"\""," rationale = \"\"\"The merge gate asks whether a lane may merge while the loop asks which review phase the lane still owes. A shared identity, evidence join, phase span and count keep both answers on the same tree and policy. Logged round evidence is authoritative because its coordinator session establishes reviewer provenance; the self-verifying trailer is only a cross-check and cannot create an approval. Identity binding answers staleness directly and prevents ordering from promoting a verdict for different work. Separate read-only and reset peels protect both contracts: the reader may traverse identity-preserving commits, while the destructive reset path may remove only the verified refresh at its tip.\"\"\""," test_refs = \"TC-205; TC-132; TC-417\""," status = \"Approved\""]},{"oldStart":3813,"oldLines":3,"newStart":3813,"newLines":14,"lines":[" status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-008\""," phase = 6","+","+[design.LLR-368]","+sr_refs = [\"SR-156\"]","+title = \"Expected-failure marks are declared, attested, and excluded from landing trees\"","+module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/red_mark.py;project-trajectory/scripts/integrate.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/verdict.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/git.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/spine.py\"","+code_symbol = \"Bars/Bars.refusal/_cause/read_bars/count/tree_counts/_removal_failures/findings/_staged_tree/_read_counts/_refusal/attest_refusal/landing_refusal;refresh;normal_test_paths/last_review_record;read_blobs;declared_roots/hidden_rel/is_test_file\"","+detail = \"The expected-failure mark is one declared non-empty stripped text beside the review bar, with no default or fallback, and both are read from one parse of the tree the verb runs on; every unavailable declaration state names the declaration, key, and cause, and when both keys are unavailable each is named. The shipped declaration carries the reference text without an at-sign and explains its required, whitespace-insensitive, other-stack, helper, and every-adopter rules. Test files are the files the review set reads: relative paths with no dot-led or __pycache__ part and a declared test-file suffix, excluding links and submodules. Counts are non-overlapping byte occurrences after ASCII whitespace is removed from the declared text and file bytes, so wrapped and parameter marks count without decoding. The reference is the newest verified review attestation in the lane range, or the lane base with no record; a test-set entry names a path only after digest normalization, never when it is a node id or directory. Equal counts are not judged. A raised count passes only when its test set names the path; a lowered count on a present path passes only when a verified reference record covers the same test set and the set names the path, otherwise each refusal names the path and failed condition; a lowered count on an absent path is not judged. An unreadable range, reference tree, or staged tree refuses naming the read. Every refusal precedes the bar and leaves branch and index unchanged. A removal made by a plain commit is judged at the next attestation. Before either refresh bar, the tree it bars refuses every marked test file with its count; a mark-free tree refreshes unchanged, a refused refresh keeps the lane at its work tip, and a refresh reads a merged declaration. Files brought by a merge-refresh are not judged; a partial close holding a mark is refused, quarantined, then refreshed; rebasing changes the base reference; and a bootstrapped scaffold receives its declaration from the template. The repository test root holds no mark in a landing tree. Coverage bound: lane attestation and refresh, a plain commit followed by attestation, merge-refresh, partial close, and declarations from the template or documented key are inside. Hand-edited attestation trailers, assertion-only stubs, differently spelled marks, trunk commits outside landing, and an individual marked test outcome are outside; a skipped test remains unmarked by procedure. After a rebase the reference is the new lane base, and earlier marks and attestations are not judged.\"","+test_refs = \"TC-421; TC-422; TC-423; TC-424; TC-425; TC-426\"","+status = \"Drafted\"","+component = \"CMP-008\"","+phase = 6"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-996\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\system-requirements.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":739,"oldLines":7,"newStart":739,"newLines":7,"lines":[" hat_refs = [\"INTEGRITY-RECOVERABILITY\", \"UNATTENDED-OPS\"]"," requirement = \"\"\"The delivered loop content shall run exactly one work item per lane on bounded, mutually isolated lanes and narrow every lane back to the integration branch through one serial, fail-closed seam that runs the declared bar on the composed tree — parking a red candidate and stopping the queue loudly, draining claiming to a clean merged stop under a declared pause, and reconstructing claim and queue state from version-control history alone at any crash boundary, never a half-integrated authoritative state.\"\"\""," rationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-027 WHOLE — ready work fans out across bounded parallel lanes and that fan-out narrows to one serialized gated seam before anything lands, in the need's own words — with SN-008 (the seam is fail-closed) and SN-025 (recovery from version-control history alone). ONE DECISION PER ROW: \"serial integration is one delivered contract\" is sound for the SEAM, but lane execution, claim authority and the trunk-side mint of work-item identity are not the seam, and a row stating the seam alone leaves SN-027's FIRST half — bounded lanes, isolated working trees, a worker ceiling — stated nowhere. This row therefore states the whole lane LIFECYCLE (claim, run isolated, close, land), which is what closes that hole; the trunk-only authority contract sheds to SR-170. The two fail independently: a perfectly serialized landing that lets a lane commit a regenerated artifact satisfies this row and not that one. Terminal close is SR-144's and is not restated here — one SR per (need, property), and both rows sit under SN-027 — so what this row carries of it is only that a terminal branch still lands through the one serial seam.\"\"\"","-acceptance_criteria = \"\"\"Every executable
